/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4.2.1  Library Location)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
630 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (MUST has one library service with two library branches and two mini libraries. The two library branches are located at both Kihumuro and City campuses. The one at the Mbarara City Campus has a sitting capacity of 700 students while the one at Kihumuro Main campus sits over 1000 students. There two mini libraries at; Faculty of Interdisciplinary Studies and Faculty of Business and Management Sciences. The library is well stocked with a collection of over 120,000 monographs with an annual addition of over 1,500 textbooks.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
631 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4.2.2  E-Resources)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
633 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4.2.3  Usage )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The library is accessible to only registered students. Every registered student shall be issued with two library cards, at the Circulation Section in the library, which he/she shall use to borrow books from the library. These cards are supposed to be kept securely because they are to be returned to the library before being cleared for graduation.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4.2.4  Library Sections )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
636 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1647 0 R
/ActualText (Circulation Section: The circulation section carries out registration of library users, issuing borrowing cards, lending and receiving books, book reservation and user education.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1648 0 R
/ActualText (Periodicals Section: This section has Serials, Journals \(print versions\), Magazines, Newspapers, Reports, Abstracts and indexes. The literature in this section is not loaned out but only read from within the library.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1649 0 R
/ActualText (Reference Sections Short Loan Section: this section has a collection of books, which are on high demand and are lent out for a short period of time to be used within the Library. The collection consists of textbooks for undergraduate and postgraduate studies based on recommendations of the academic staff and departments.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1650 0 R
/ActualText (The Book Bank Section: This is a section where books are lent out to users for a long period of time usually a whole semester.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1651 0 R
/ActualText (Discussion Rooms: At Kihumuro Campus main Library, there are discussion rooms where groups of students can book and study or discuss in their study groups.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1652 0 R
/ActualText (Research Carrels: At Kihumuro Campus Main Library still, there are research carrels where graduate students and researchers can book and patronize these quiet individualized spaces for their private study or research. There are some that are served on first come first served basis, while others can be booked for a week or a month.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
642 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1653 0 R
/ActualText (Institutional Repository: MUST library has an institutional repository that can be accessed on ir.must.ac.ug. This is a platform where the library collects all research conducted by the MUST graduate students and staff in form of dissertations, journal articles, books and book chapters.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
